# Third-party notices — LockedIn desktop

This file inventories what the desktop artifact distributes and where its
notices live. It records facts only; the licence texts it points at are the
generated ones, not copies.

Artifact: `dist/lockedin-desktop-linux-x64.tar.gz`, rendered from
`desktop/build/linux/x64/release/bundle/`. Audit and findings:
`desktop/docs/licensing.md` §Audit.

## Application

LockedIn — **AGPL-3.0-only**. Full text: `LICENSE`. `scripts/desktop-package.sh`
copies it to the archive root and verifies it is present.

## Flutter shell and Dart packages

Bundle entries: `lockedin_desktop`, `lib/libapp.so`,
`lib/libflutter_linux_gtk.so`, `lib/libfile_selector_linux_plugin.so`,
`data/icudtl.dat`, `data/flutter_assets/**`.

Notices: **`data/flutter_assets/NOTICES.Z`**, generated by
`flutter build linux --release` (103 231 bytes, 115 named components). It carries
the licence texts for the Flutter framework and engine (BSD-3-Clause), the Dart
SDK and core libraries, the engine's bundled third-party libraries (Skia, ICU,
BoringSSL, zlib, HarfBuzz, FreeType, libpng, libjpeg-turbo, libwebp, libjxl,
Expat, Vulkan components …) and every Dart package compiled into `libapp.so`,
including `material_ui` 1.11.0, `cupertino_ui` 1.1.6, `file_selector` 1.1.0 and
its platform packages (BSD-3-Clause), `cupertino_icons` 1.0.9 (MIT) and the
transitive `intl`, `http`, `vector_math`, `material_color_utilities`
(Apache-2.0), `collection`, `characters`, `meta`, `typed_data`, `web`.

## Bun core sidecar

`lockedin-core` is `bun build --compile` output: the Bun runtime plus the
application modules and the npm packages it imports, compiled in. No
`node_modules` directory is distributed.

Notices: **`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`** (repository root), generated by
`bun run scripts/licenses.ts` from `bun.lock` and verified by
`tests/unit/licenses.test.ts`. It reproduces the Bun runtime notice, the notice
for the libraries Bun statically links (including JavaScriptCore/WebKit, LGPL-2),
and the licence texts of the bundled npm packages — `ai` and the `@ai-sdk/*`
family, `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `zod`, `ajv`, `fflate`, `smol-toml`,
`zod-to-json-schema`, `which`, `cross-spawn` and their transitive packages
(Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-3-Clause, ISC). `licenses/BUN-LICENSE.md` is the Bun text
that file embeds.

The native keychain addon `@napi-rs/keyring` (MIT) is **not** redistributed: the
bundle contains no `.node` file, so the core falls back to the `secret-tool`
command shim on Linux and ships no addon binary.

## Shipped today, and the gap

Inside the tarball:

- `LICENSE` — the app licence (AGPL-3.0-only);
- `data/flutter_assets/NOTICES.Z` — the Flutter/Dart/engine notice set.

**Not shipped:** `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` and this `NOTICE`. `NOTICES.Z` is
generated by Flutter and says nothing about Bun or the npm packages in
`lockedin-core`, so a release today is missing the sidecar's notices.
`scripts/desktop-package.sh` must stage both files into the bundle and add them
to its `REQUIRED` list before a public release; that is tracked in
`desktop/tasks/T-007-qa.md`.
